 SG_ LAT_STOCK_TORQUE_44_REQUEST_3 : 132|1@0+ (1,0) [0|1] "" BMW_I3
CM_ BO_ 44 "Stock lateral torque/control candidate on the vehicle-side companion stream. Route 58/59 TJA-window analysis points to bytes 13..14 signed little-endian as the strongest local equivalent to 0x33/src1 steering output. Firmware injection follows the I-CAN-hack raw override model: trigger 0x42, target 0x44, cycle mask 0x01, base 0, copy payload bytes 1..16, direction FR3, then update only the FlexRay header cycle/count CRC. Host/openpilot must compute payload CRCs byte1=crc8(byte2..8, init 0xA4) and byte9=crc8(byte10..16, init 0xDC).";
CM_ SG_ 44 LAT_STOCK_TORQUE_44_RAW "Primary local torque/control-like value: raw = int16_le(byte13, byte14). Correlation against 0x33/src1 bytes 3..4 inside managed TJA windows was about +0.847 on route 58 and +0.916 on route 59.";
CM_ SG_ 44 LAT_STOCK_TORQUE_44_ALT_WORD_10_11 "Secondary debug word from bytes 10..11. Keep only for comparison while reconstructing the full 0x44 payload.";
CM_ SG_ 44 LAT_STOCK_TORQUE_44_ALT_WORD_12_13 "Secondary debug word from bytes 12..13. It correlates less consistently than bytes 13..14 and is not the selected torque value.";
CM_ SG_ 44 LAT_STOCK_TORQUE_44_ALT_WORD_14_15 "Secondary debug word from bytes 14..15. Keep only for comparison while reconstructing the full 0x44 payload.";
CM_ SG_ 44 LAT_STOCK_TORQUE_44_ICAN_HACK_NM "Reference layout from I-CAN-hack pico-flexray 0x44 EPS_CONTROL torque field: 12-bit unsigned at byte11/bit88, factor 0.005, offset -10 Nm. Included as a cross-check, not selected over the local b13..14 route fit.";
CM_ SG_ 44 LAT_STOCK_TORQUE_44_CHECKSUM_1 "Application CRC for the first 0x44 payload block. Host must set this to crc8(payload bytes 2..8, init 0xA4); firmware raw override does not recalculate it.";
CM_ SG_ 44 LAT_STOCK_TORQUE_44_CHECKSUM_2 "Application CRC for the second 0x44 payload block. Host must set this to crc8(payload bytes 10..16, init 0xDC); firmware raw override does not recalculate it.";
CM_ SG_ 44 LAT_STOCK_TORQUE_44_MODE "I-CAN-hack EPS_CONTROL torque mode field. Their script uses 2 when active, mostly 14 otherwise.";
CM_ SG_ 44 LAT_STOCK_TORQUE_44_MODE_COPY "Mirror of LAT_STOCK_TORQUE_44_MODE in the I-CAN-hack EPS_CONTROL layout.";
CM_ SG_ 44 LAT_STOCK_TORQUE_44_LKA_STATE "I-CAN-hack EPS_CONTROL LKA state field. Observed/scripted behavior ramps through 0..14 on engage/disengage and typically stays around 5..9 while active.";
CM_ SG_ 44 LAT_STOCK_TORQUE_44_REQUEST_2 "I-CAN-hack EPS_CONTROL request state: 1 inactive, 2 active.";
CM_ SG_ 44 LAT_STOCK_TORQUE_44_REQUEST_3 "I-CAN-hack EPS_CONTROL request bit. Their script sets it to 1 only while not ramping up/down and active.";
VAL_ 44 LAT_STOCK_TORQUE_44_REQUEST_2 1 "INACTIVE" 2 "ACTIVE";

BO_ 60 LAT_STOCK_TX_TRIGGER_CANDIDATE: 17 BMW_I3
 SG_ LAT_STOCK_TRIGGER_PHASE_BYTE_0 : 0|8@1+ (1,0) [0|255] "" BMW_I3
