CM_ BO_ 60 "Primary SAS-side predecessor/trigger for the stock lateral burst on the i3. Latest route work now treats frame 96 as the active payload candidate. Frame 60 itself remains structurally near-empty outside byte0, so treat it as the scheduler/trigger half of the burst rather than the analog steering payload.";
CM_ SG_ 60 LAT_STOCK_TRIGGER_PHASE_BYTE_0 "Raw scheduler byte for the SAS-side lateral burst. This remains the practical trigger byte for firmware-aligned injection work.";
CM_ SG_ 60 LAT_STOCK_TRIGGER_SUBFRAME_LSB "Low two bits of frame-60 byte0. Useful when reconstructing the four-subframe burst order observed in the SAS 20 ms lateral scheduler.";
CM_ SG_ 60 LAT_STOCK_TRIGGER_CMD_PHASE "Derived command-phase view of frame-60 byte0 (byte0 >> 1). Keep as a coarse scheduler helper while the real command stays phase-local on frame 96.";

