CM_ BO_ 135 "Primary longitudinal/lateral session-state helper, but no longer a single rigid TJA gate. Historical labeling from 000003ff/00000400/00000402 still holds for the older families: manual -> ...22e0e188a205, ACC-only -> ...2228e260a205, older TJA -> ...2228e2604206 / ...20e0e2403206. Newer realdata route 00000006--e6a3e58043 shows additional valid managed-TJA families that do not fit the old 4206-only rule, especially ...20e0e240e201, ...2228e260e201, ...2228e2608202, and ...2228e2408202. Use 135 together with the 60->72 burst behavior when classifying stock lateral context; 135 alone is no longer sufficient to declare ACC-only vs TJA on newer routes. Draft lateral work: on routes 00000401, 00000402, and 00000006, byte1 on this frame is the best current common CAN-only precursor for stock lateral steering activity inside the true lateral windows defined by 0x10D/src0/byte11 == 1.";
CM_ SG_ 135 LAT_DRAFT_087_BYTE0 "Draft helper only. Byte0 behaves like a 16-state phase/counter byte and does not currently decode to steering content.";
CM_ SG_ 135 LAT_DRAFT_087_BYTE1 "Draft helper only. Best current common src0 lateral precursor candidate across routes 401, 402, and 006 when evaluated event-by-event inside the true lateral windows (0x10D/src0/byte11 == 1). Treat as a coded/discrete byte, not an analog steering angle.";
CM_ SG_ 135 LAT_DRAFT_087_BYTE2 "Draft helper only. Byte2 behaves like a rolling phase byte and does not currently decode to steering content.";
CM_ SG_ 135 LAT_DRAFT_087_DIR_CODE "Draft derived direction code from byte1 low 6 bits. Experimental family rule that currently works around 75% on routes 401, 402, and 006: if (old_byte1 & 0x3F) > 44 then steer right, else steer left. This is not yet a final actuator rule.";

