 SG_ LAT_TJA_STATE_10D : 88|8@1+ (1,0) [0|255] "" BMW_I3
CM_ BO_ 269 "Experimental helper from legacy multi-segment TJA routes 00000054/55/56. Modern route 00000401 identifies byte11 on this frame as the best current stock lateral-TJA state candidate. EDME/EPS route 00000058 confirms the same byte as a clean TJA managed-window indicator: rlog dat[11] changed 0->1 at 8.373s, 1->0 at 88.359s, 0->1 at 118.868s, and 1->0 at 153.652s, matching the video-marked TJA windows after the camera/rlog offset. EDME/EPS route 00000059 confirms the same rule after ecamera/fcamera alignment: dat[11] entered state 1 at 158.034s and left state 1 at 239.663s, matching the user-verified TJA managed video window. Keep the rest of the payload raw until the full frame is understood.";
CM_ SG_ 269 LAT_TJA_STATE_10D "Best current stock TJA state candidate on frame 0x10D byte11. Current working semantics: 0 = TJA steering button/path not requested; 2 = TJA armed; 3 = TJA longitudinal only active; 1 = TJA managed/lateral-active window confirmed on EDME routes 58/59 and LONG_AND_LATERAL_ACTIVE on previous routes. State 8 marks driver steering override and may also appear when the lead vehicle disappears or becomes too distant for TJA to keep the lateral function engaged. State 16 marks a TJA prerequisite violation or operating-limit violation, for example missing steering-wheel touch or requested curvature outside the valid operating envelope. RX analysis note only: do not use this DBC entry as a TX activation command or synthesize activation from it.";
 VAL_ 269 LAT_TJA_STATE_10D 0 "STEERING_NOT_REQUESTED" 1 "LONG_AND_LATERAL_ACTIVE" 2 "TJA_ARMED" 3 "LONGITUDINAL_ONLY_ACTIVE" 8 "DRIVER_STEERING_OVERRIDE" 16 "PREREQUISITE_OR_OPERATING_LIMIT_VIOLATION";

